        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60535,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60536,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "<p>The locations are similar to those of conventional chordoma, predominantly in sacrococcygeal sites {21184634}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-10T11:46:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60537,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "<h5><em>Signs and symptoms</em></h5>\r\n<p>The symptoms are similar to those of conventional chordoma, although progression may be more rapid. Pain and site-related neurological symptoms are common. Dedifferentiated chordoma&nbsp;may present de novo or at a location of a previously resected conventional chordoma.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Imaging</em></h5>\r\n<p>Dedifferentiated chordomas show morphology similar to that of conventional tumours and cannot be distinguished on radiographs or CT. A bimorphic appearance may be appreciated on MRI, with the dedifferentiated component suggested by areas of tumour that are relatively hypointense on T2-weighted imaging&nbsp;/ fluid-sensitive studies, distinct from the typically T2-hyperintense conventional chordoma {18450635}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-27T14:28:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60538,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dedifferentiated chordoma is the rarest notochordal tumour subtype, with only case reports and small series published {18450635; 2440324; 17630110; 6095644}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60539,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60540,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/33/166\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Conventional chordoma</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-19T16:22:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60541,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour presents as a large mass with a biphasic appearance. The dedifferentiated component has the gross features of a high-grade sarcoma with a solid surface, juxtaposed to a gelatinous and myxoid conventional chordoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60542,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "<p>The distinguishing characteristic is the simultaneous presence of a conventional chordoma and a high-grade spindle and/or pleomorphic sarcoma. Osteosarcomatous and rhabdomyosarcomatous differentiation can be seen. The two components are usually abruptly separated, but they can be intermingled.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h5>\r\n<p>The dedifferentiated component can show focal cytokeratin expression but does not express brachyury {16538613}. Specific lineages, such as rhabdomyoblastic, should be supported by immunohistochemical expression of desmin and myogenin.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Differential diagnosis</em></h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes dedifferentiated chondrosarcoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-19T10:04:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60543,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60544,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No diagnostic molecular markers have been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60545,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone tumour with compatible imaging; conventional chordoma (histologically or by history) plus high-grade sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60546,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "<p>Staging is according to bone sarcoma protocols (see &lt;&lt;TNM-Bone&gt;&gt;<em>TNM staging of tumours of bone</em>). See also the information on staging in <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/33/261\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Bone tumours: Introduction</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-19T16:22:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 60547,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 257,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is poor; the metastatic rate and mortality are high. The benefits of chemotherapy or radiotherapy seem negligible. Surgery is the only option.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-11-26T16:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]